"[{\"name\":\"Goblet Squat\",\"description\":\"Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart, then bend your knees and lower your body down until your thighs are parallel to the ground. Push through your heels to return to standing.\",\"difficulty\":\"Beginner\",\"sets\":3,\"reps\":\"8-12\",\"benefits\":\"Improves strength and flexibility in the legs, glutes, and lower back; enhances balance and coordination.\",\"image\":30,\"youtubeVideoId\":\"dQw4w9WgXcQ\",\"id\":\"1743793555220\",\"dateAdded\":\"2025-04-04T19:05:55.220Z\",\"bodyPart\":\"Lower Legs\",\"exerciseType\":\"Free Weight\"},{\"name\":\"Dumbbell Step-Up\",\"description\":\"Stand in front of a step or platform, then lift one foot up onto the step and bring the other foot up to meet it. Lower your body back down to the starting position and repeat with the other leg.\",\"difficulty\":\"Beginner/Moderate\",\"sets\":3,\"reps\":\"8-12 per leg\",\"benefits\":\"Improves strength and balance in the legs, glutes, and lower back; enhances cardiovascular fitness.\",\"image\":30,\"youtubeVideoId\":\"dQw4w9WgXcQ\",\"id\":\"1743793552492\",\"dateAdded\":\"2025-04-04T19:05:52.492Z\",\"bodyPart\":\"Lower Legs\",\"exerciseType\":\"Free Weight\"},{\"name\":\"Overhead Dumbbell Extension Machine\",\"description\":\"Sit at an overhead dumbbell extension machine with your back against the pad, then grasp the bar with your hands shoulder-width apart. Lift the weight up by extending your arms, keeping your upper arms still and only moving your forearms.\",\"difficulty\":\"Advanced\",\"sets\":3,\"reps\":8,\"benefits\":\"Works triceps for increased strength and muscle mass.\",\"image\":30,\"youtubeVideoId\":\"f8H9L2zUxgY\",\"id\":\"1743793021205\",\"dateAdded\":\"2025-04-04T18:57:01.205Z\",\"bodyPart\":\"Arms\",\"exerciseType\":\"Machine\"},{\"name\":\"Bicep Curl Machine\",\"description\":\"Sit at a bicep curl machine with your back against the pad, then grasp the bar with your hands shoulder-width apart. Lift the weight up by curling your arms, keeping your upper arms still and only moving your forearms.\",\"difficulty\":\"Beginner\",\"sets\":3,\"reps\":10,\"benefits\":\"Works biceps for increased strength and muscle mass.\",\"image\":30,\"youtubeVideoId\":\"g2G9Tf0yVU8\",\"id\":\"1743793017518\",\"dateAdded\":\"2025-04-04T18:56:57.518Z\",\"bodyPart\":\"Arms\",\"exerciseType\":\"Machine\"},{\"name\":\"Standing Calf Raise Machine\",\"description\":\"Position yourself under the shoulder pads of the machine, adjusting the height so you are standing tall when your heels are flat. Place the balls of your feet on the edge of the platform with your heels hanging off. Keep your knees slightly bent (not locked) and your core engaged for stability. Stand tall, pushing the pads up slightly with your shoulders to support the weight. Slowly lower your heels as far as comfortable, feeling a deep stretch in your calves. Drive through the balls of your feet to raise your heels as high as possible, contracting your calf muscles (gastrocnemius) intensely at the top. Hold briefly, then slowly return to the stretched position.\",\"difficulty\":\"Beginner/Moderate\",\"sets\":\"3\",\"reps\":\"10-15\",\"benefits\":\"Primarily targets the gastrocnemius (the larger, upper part of the calf), improving explosive power for activities like jumping and running, enhancing calf definition, and increasing overall lower leg strength.\",\"image\":{\"uri\":\"https://images.pexels.com/photos/669576/pexels-photo-669576.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1260&h=750&dpr=1\"},\"youtubeVideoId\":\"YMmgqO8Jo-k\",\"id\":\"1743658014562\",\"dateAdded\":\"2025-04-03T05:26:54.562Z\",\"bodyPart\":\"Lower Legs\",\"exerciseType\":\"Machine\"},{\"name\":\"Seated Dumbbell Calf Raise\",\"description\":\"Sit on the edge of a bench with your feet flat on the floor (or balls of feet on a small elevated block/plate for greater range of motion). Place a dumbbell vertically on each knee, holding them securely. Keeping your back straight, press through the balls of your feet to lift your heels as high as possible, contracting your calf muscles. Hold the peak contraction for a moment. Slowly lower your heels back down until you feel a stretch in your calves. Repeat.\",\"difficulty\":\"Beginner/Moderate\",\"sets\":\"3-4\",\"reps\":\"15-25\",\"benefits\":\"Primarily targets the soleus (lower calf) muscle due to the bent-knee position, improves calf endurance and contributes to overall lower leg development.\",\"image\":{\"uri\":\"https://www.inspireusafoundation.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/seated-dumbbell-calf-raise.png\"},\"youtubeVideoId\":\"Ngg_9j_a-fQ\",\"id\":\"1743542828628\",\"dateAdded\":\"2025-04-01T21:27:08.628Z\",\"bodyPart\":\"Lower Legs\",\"exerciseType\":\"Free Weight\"},{\"name\":\"Seated Hip Abduction\",\"description\":\"Sit comfortably on the machine with your back straight and pressed against the back pad. Place the outside of your lower thighs or knees against the machine's pads. Ensure your feet are placed securely on the footrests. Begin the movement by slowly pushing your legs outwards against the pads, focusing on contracting your outer hip and glute muscles. Push as far as comfortably possible. Pause briefly at the peak contraction, then slowly and controllably return your legs to the starting position. Avoid using momentum or letting the weight stack slam.\",\"difficulty\":\"Beginner\",\"sets\":\"3\",\"reps\":\"12-15\",\"benefits\":\"Strengthens the hip abductor muscles (gluteus medius and minimus), which helps improve hip stability, balance, and can contribute to better walking/running mechanics and potentially reduce knee valgus (knees collapsing inward).\",\"image\":{\"uri\":\"https://cdn.pixabay.com/photo/2017/04/27/08/29/sport-2264825_1280.jpg\"},\"youtubeVideoId\":\"0c9Jw__pL68\",\"id\":\"1743532394254\",\"dateAdded\":\"2025-04-01T18:33:14.254Z\",\"bodyPart\":\"Hips\",\"exerciseType\":\"Machine\"},{\"name\":\"Dumbbell Flyes\",\"description\":\"Lie flat on a bench with feet firmly planted on the floor. Hold a dumbbell in each hand directly above your chest, palms facing each other. Maintain a slight, constant bend in your elbows throughout the movement. Slowly lower the dumbbells out to your sides in a wide arc, feeling a stretch across your chest. Lower until the dumbbells are roughly level with your chest or shoulders. Squeeze your chest muscles (pectoralis major) to bring the dumbbells back up along the same arc to the starting position. Avoid letting the dumbbells touch at the top to maintain tension.\",\"difficulty\":\"Moderate\",\"sets\":\"3\",\"reps\":\"10-15\",\"benefits\":\"Isolates the chest muscles, particularly focusing on the stretching and adduction (bringing arms toward the midline) function. Helps develop chest width and improves the mind-muscle connection with the pecs.\",\"image\":{\"uri\":\"https://images.pexels.com/photos/669578/pexels-photo-669578.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1260&h=750&dpr=1\"},\"youtubeVideoId\":\"Qc4hR0_m41o\",\"id\":\"1743530800593\",\"dateAdded\":\"2025-04-01T18:06:40.593Z\",\"bodyPart\":\"Chest\",\"exerciseType\":\"Free Weight\"},{\"name\":\"Machine Lateral Raise\",\"description\":\"Adjust the seat height so the machine's pivot points align with your shoulder joints when seated. Sit facing forward, typically with your chest against a pad if provided. Place the outside of your upper arms or forearms (depending on machine design) against the padded levers. Your elbows should have a slight bend. Exhale and abduct your arms, pushing the levers outward and upward until your upper arms are roughly parallel to the floor. Focus on using your side deltoids to lift the weight, minimizing momentum. Pause briefly at the peak contraction. Inhale as you slowly lower the levers back to the starting position under control.\",\"difficulty\":\"Beginner\",\"sets\":\"3\",\"reps\":\"12-15\",\"benefits\":\"Effectively isolates and strengthens the medial (side) deltoids, contributing to shoulder width and a V-taper appearance. The machine guides the movement path, helping to ensure proper form and consistent tension on the target muscle.\",\"image\":{\"uri\":\"https://images.pexels.com/photos/6550874/pexels-photo-6550874.jpeg\"},\"youtubeVideoId\":\"3_J-je6P_Ms\",\"id\":\"1743530160631\",\"dateAdded\":\"2025-04-01T17:56:00.631Z\",\"bodyPart\":\"Shoulders\",\"exerciseType\":\"Machine\"},{\"name\":\"Machine Shoulder Press\",\"description\":\"Sit upright on the machine with your back firmly against the pad. Adjust the seat height so the handles are approximately level with your shoulders. Grasp the handles with an overhand grip (palms facing forward). Plant your feet firmly on the floor. Exhale as you press the handles directly overhead until your arms are nearly fully extended, but avoid locking out your elbows. Pause briefly at the top. Inhale as you slowly lower the handles back to the starting position, maintaining control throughout the movement. Ensure your back remains pressed against the pad and avoid arching.\",\"difficulty\":\"Beginner\",\"sets\":\"3\",\"reps\":\"10-15\",\"benefits\":\"Builds strength and muscle mass primarily in the anterior (front) and medial (side) deltoids, as well as the triceps. The machine provides stability, making it a safer option for beginners or those focusing on controlled movement, helping improve overhead pressing strength.\",\"image\":{\"uri\":\"https://images.pexels.com/photos/6550851/pexels-photo-6550851.jpeg\"},\"youtubeVideoId\":\"DeGg_c_eA6E\",\"id\":\"1743530157533\",\"dateAdded\":\"2025-04-01T17:55:57.535Z\",\"bodyPart\":\"Shoulders\",\"exerciseType\":\"Machine\"},{\"name\":\"Seated Calf Raise Machine\",\"description\":\"Sit on the machine with the balls of your feet firmly on the platform edge, heels hanging off. Place the padded lever just above your knees. Release the safety bar. Lower your heels as far as comfortably possible to feel a stretch in your calves. Push through the balls of your feet to raise your heels as high as possible, squeezing your calf muscles at the top. Hold briefly, then slowly lower back down. Maintain control throughout the movement.\",\"difficulty\":\"Beginner\",\"sets\":\"3\",\"reps\":\"12-15\",\"benefits\":\"Primarily targets the soleus muscle in the lower leg, contributing to calf size and endurance. Also strengthens the gastrocnemius. Improves ankle stability.\",\"image\":{\"uri\":\"https://images.pexels.com/photos/669578/pexels-photo-669578.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1260&h=750&dpr=1\"},\"youtubeVideoId\":\"JbyjN43c_9I\",\"id\":\"1743529369286\",\"dateAdded\":\"2025-04-01T17:42:49.286Z\",\"bodyPart\":\"Lower Legs\",\"exerciseType\":\"Machine\"},{\"name\":\"Standing Calf Raise Machine\",\"description\":\"Position yourself in a standing calf raise machine with the shoulder pads resting comfortably on your shoulders. Place the balls of your feet on the platform edge, heels hanging off. Keep your knees slightly bent (not locked) and your core engaged. Lower your heels slowly, feeling a stretch in your calves. Then, push through the balls of your feet to raise your heels as high as possible, contracting your calf muscles. Hold the peak contraction briefly before slowly lowering back down.\",\"difficulty\":\"Beginner/Moderate\",\"sets\":\"3\",\"reps\":\"10-15\",\"benefits\":\"Targets both the gastrocnemius (upper/outer calf) and soleus muscles. Builds calf strength and size, improves jumping ability and ankle strength.\",\"image\":{\"uri\":\"https://www.muscleandfitness.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Machine-Calf-Raise.jpg?quality=86&strip=all\"},\"youtubeVideoId\":\"YMmgqO8Jo-k\",\"id\":\"1743529365739\",\"dateAdded\":\"2025-04-01T17:42:45.739Z\",\"bodyPart\":\"Lower Legs\",\"exerciseType\":\"Machine\"},{\"name\":\"Seated Chest Press Machine\",\"description\":\"Sit on the machine with your back flat against the pad. Adjust the seat height so the handles are level with the middle of your chest. Plant your feet firmly on the floor. Grasp the handles with a full grip, palms facing down. Exhale and push the handles forward until your arms are fully extended but not locked. Keep your back pressed against the pad. Inhale and slowly return the handles to the starting position, controlling the weight throughout the movement. Avoid letting the weight stack touch down between reps.\",\"difficulty\":\"Beginner\",\"sets\":\"3\",\"reps\":\"8-12\",\"benefits\":\"Builds strength and muscle mass in the pectoralis major (chest), anterior deltoids (front shoulders), and triceps. Provides stability, making it a safe option for beginners.\",\"imageUrl\":\"https://images.pexels.com/photos/1552106/pexels-photo-1552106.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1260&h=750&dpr=1\",\"youtubeVideoId\":\"rXwgc-S5UeQ\",\"image\":{\"uri\":\"https://images.pexels.com/photos/1552106/pexels-photo-1552106.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1260&h=750&dpr=1\"},\"id\":\"1743528716872\",\"dateAdded\":\"2025-04-01T17:31:56.872Z\",\"bodyPart\":\"Chest\",\"exerciseType\":\"Machine\"},{\"name\":\"Leg Press\",\"description\":\"Sit in a leg press machine with your feet shoulder-width apart on the platform. Push the platform away from you, extending your legs. Then, slowly lower the platform back down to the starting position.\",\"difficulty\":\"Moderate\",\"sets\":3,\"reps\":8,\"benefits\":\"Works quadriceps, hamstrings, and glutes; improves leg strength and stability\",\"image\":30,\"youtubeVideoId\":\"l3xVd2PzGqU\",\"id\":\"1743794881568\",\"dateAdded\":\"2025-04-04T19:28:01.568Z\",\"bodyPart\":\"Lower Legs\",\"exerciseType\":\"Machine\"}]"